  "limits": [
    "The four targets and both stored regions are file-relative measurements under the reference mapping.",
    "This establishes stored extents and a size-valued field read by ARM code. The executed path, D11 destination, and exact transfer count remain unobserved.",
    "The nonzero-prefix and all-zero-suffix counts are structural. Logical treatment of zero records and the contemporary D11 instruction fields remain open."
  ],
  "method": {
    "anchor_and_pool": "Use the Linux BCM4378 RAM-origin model to form the modeled first-window start and search aligned LE32 words before the first window. Require a unique occurrence and compare the preceding three consecutive four-byte slots. Translate all resulting values back to file offsets under the same model.",
    "component_bounds": "Measure the two intervals between the first start and the intervening field, and between the second start and the following boundary. Count leading nonzero LE64 records then trailing all-zero records and verify byte 7 of each complete record is zero.",
    "input": "The three stock BCM4378 files and their original record windows from 2026-11-17-d11-window-profile.json, verified by whole-file SHA-256",
    "reader_check": "Scan two-byte boundaries within 4096 bytes of each literal slot for Thumb LDR (literal) T1 and T2 encodings that resolve to the slot. Confirm instruction kind and PC-relative addressing by individually decoding the matching T1 candidate with Rizin 0.9.1 in Thumb mode.",
    "size_read_check": "In the four-instruction block beginning at the size-field reference, verify the first-component literal read is next, then a word load dereferences the size-field pointer before a branch. Separately verify the following-boundary and second-component references are decoded as consecutive instructions.",
    "sources": {
      "linux_bcm4378_ram_model": "https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.12/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/chip.c",
